# Kino License

Copyright (c) 2026 Kino (kinotvapp) — https://github.com/kinotvapp/kino-light

Kino's source code is public so that people can read it and learn from it. It is not open source:
you may not copy it into another app, redistribute it (modified or not) or use it commercially.

## 1. Which license covers which files

- **MIT License** — everything under these directories, each of which carries its own `LICENSE` file:
  - `plugins/sdk/` (the plugin kit)
  - `plugins/archive-org/` (the example plugin)
  - `docs/plugins/` (the plugin guide, contract and reference files)
- **Third-party code** — keeps its own license. `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` lists every such file, its
  origin and the file that holds its license text.
- **Everything else in this repository** (the "software" in the terms below) — the
  **PolyForm Strict License 1.0.0**, reproduced unchanged at the end of this file, together with the
  additional permissions in section 2.

## 2. Additional permissions

The licensor grants these permissions in addition to the PolyForm Strict License 1.0.0. They do not
change its text, and every other limit in it still applies.

1. **Building and running.** You may build the software from this repository and install and run
   what you build on devices you own or control, for any permitted purpose. Building the software is
   not, by itself, making changes or new works based on it.
2. **Contributing.** You may make changes to the software only to propose them for inclusion in this
   repository (for example, a fork on GitHub and a pull request to `kinotvapp/kino-light`), and run
   those changes on your own devices to test them. You may not distribute a changed version in any
   other way: no builds, APKs, app-store listings or copies of the code in another project.
3. **Contributions you send.** When you submit a contribution to this repository, you license it to
   the licensor under the MIT License, so it can be included in the software under these or any
   other terms, and you confirm you have the right to do so.

## 3. Versions published earlier

Versions of this repository that were published under the Apache License 2.0 before this file
replaced it stay available under that license for those versions. These terms apply to everything
published from this change on.

